text:
I'll keep this round focused on concrete commitments. Austria needs reassurance about Tyrolia. France needs a clean border confirmation. Turkey is already aligned. No need to message Germany, England, or Russia this round.

MESSAGES:
{
  "AUSTRIA": "Final commitment: F NAP - ION, A VEN - TYR, A ROM H. TYR is purely a transit position — I have no orders pointing at TRI or VIE this year. If you're moving A VIE or A BUD east toward Serbia/Rumania, we won't interfere with each other at all.",
  "FRANCE": "Final commitment from me: A VEN goes to TYR, not PIE. I expect you to keep A MAR out of PIE and F BRE away from the Ligurian coast. Clean border, both of us grow elsewhere."
}

Looking at the board, I need to secure SPA and push into GAS this fall. England is moving F ENG toward Belgium — I need to decide if I'll contest Belgium now or let England have it. Germany wants Holland and is asking if I'm going for it. I should clarify that Holland is Germany's while asking them to stay out of BEL. I also need to make sure England knows I won't interfere with their NTH→BEL move this turn, but I want to set up for BEL in 1902.

MESSAGES:
{
  "ENGLAND": "Good — I'll stay out of Belgium this fall. Take it if you want. I'm just securing GAS and POR in the southwest. For 1902, let's talk Belgium then — I may want a piece of it, but we can work something out.",
  "GERMANY": "Holland is yours, no interference from me. I'm just taking GAS and POR this fall — well south of your borders. For 1902, I'd like to discuss Belgium as a shared interest; we should coordinate on that rather than race each other."
}

The situation has shifted: Austria won't commit A SER to RUM this spring (it's fighting Italy for Trieste), so a coordinated RUM strike isn't on. Russia is committing north/west, leaving F RUM and SEV thin. With Austria distracted and Russia looking away, I have a real opening. But attacking RUM alone — A BUL - RUM plus F ANK - BLA convoy support — could work since F RUM is isolated (only A UKR backs it, and Russia says UKR is going to Warsaw). Actually if I move F ANK to BLA and A BUL to RUM, F RUM defends with strength 1, my A BUL attacks with 1 (no support) = bounce. I need BLA fleet supporting BUL into RUM. Let me lean on Russia's diversion: lull Russia, then strike RUM. I'll mislead Russia one more round while setting up the stab.

MESSAGES:
{
  "RUSSIA": "Agreed, DMZ extends — F ANK stays out of BLA and ARM stays clear of SEV this spring. Push hard on Warsaw and Norway; you have my eastern flank quiet. Let's both grow outward.",
  "AUSTRIA": "Understood — you secure TRI this spring and we hit RUM together in the fall. I'll hold my position in BUL and keep ARM poised so we strike clean once your SER is free. Tell me the moment TRI is yours and I'll bring full weight to RUM."
}

I need to commit to the RUM strike with Austria. The key risk is Austria stabbing into BUL, or Russia having lied about F RUM holding. Russia explicitly said F RUM holds and nothing enters BLA — that makes my strike land cleanly with surprise. I'll lock in with Austria one final time.

MESSAGES:
{
  "AUSTRIA": "Locked: I move A BUL - RUM, F ANK - BLA S A BUL - RUM. You must order A SER - RUM with A GAL S A SER - RUM — three attackers, F RUM falls even with A UKR support. Do NOT touch BUL; if you step on my home flank the strike collapses and Italy takes BUD behind you. Whoever's adjacent claims RUM in Winter — I'll hold it with my unit there.",
  "RUSSIA": "Final word: I'm keeping ARM clear of SEV and my northern intentions toward you unchanged — focus everything on Warsaw and Norway, that's where Germany is hurting you."
}

This is the final round. I hold SEV, BLA, ARM, and want to take RUM. Russia is moving F RUM→SEV with A MOS support, which means RUM will be vacated — I can walk F SEV or F BLA into RUM. But if Russia attacks SEV with two units (F RUM + A MOS support), I'd lose SEV unless I defend. Better: I move F BLA→RUM (RUM vacates as F RUM moves to SEV), and defend SEV. Austria offered F BUL/SC support — I can use it to back F SEV holding or my BLA→RUM. Let me lock in a concrete deal with Austria to support BLA→RUM, and keep ARM defending SEV.

MESSAGES:
{
  "AUSTRIA": "Concrete: I'm taking RUM this turn — F BLA - RUM. Commit F BUL/SC S F BLA - RUM and Rumania falls cleanly, clearing Russia's fleet from your eastern flank entirely. In return I keep my fleets off the Aegean and we face Italy together next year.",
  "RUSSIA": "You're sending F RUM to SEV, which vacates Rumania — I'm taking RUM. If you insist on the fight, you lose RUM and gain nothing while Germany eats your north. Pull A MOS off SEV support and I'll leave your home alone after RUM; that's the only de-escalation left."
}
